            <ArticleTitle>Simple and innovative method of removal of unfavourable root: technical note.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>49475517742218</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/0049475517742218</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Extraction of teeth is one of the most commonly performed minor oral surgical procedures. However, some clinical situations render routine extractions challenging. Here we report such a situation and a simple and innovative technique that involves the use of braided stainless steel wire to remove an unfavorable palatally inclined left upper lateral incisor with least damage to adjacent structures.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
